; A typed WebAssembly (core 2.0 scalar subset) representation: value types,
; numeric operations, a structural validator and a deterministic binary
; encoder. Nothing here knows the Loop IR, so a second producer needs no
; tensor or graph library. See the Wasm backend design doc in .ai/.
;
; Wrapped false with a [wasm_] prefix on every module, as [js_ast] is. Depends
; on [err_trace] and [fmt] only, and is JS-reachable, so the integer rule
; applies: every immediate that can reach 2^31 is an [int32]/[int64], and no
; length or constant is ever held in a 63-bit [int] unchecked.

(library
 (name wasm_ir)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries err_trace fmt))
